  <running_head>P. VOET</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">injustè se condemnatum iri,</l>
    <l n="2">quòd ejus adversarius superior</l>
    <l n="3">in judicio sit futurus, idque te-</l>
    <l n="4">stibus falsis in medium pro-</l>
    <l n="5">latis : attamen existumarem</l>
    <l n="6">non licere parti innocenti du-</l>
    <l n="7">ello adversarium iniquum pro-</l>
    <l n="8">vocare , multò minùs per insi-</l>
    <l n="9">dias, vel occultè è medio tolle-</l>
    <l n="10">re. Ratio civilis est, quia non est</l>
    <l n="11">concedendum singulis, quod</l>
    <l n="12">per magistratum publicè fieri</l>
    <l n="13">potest, ne occasio sit majoris</l>
    <l n="14">tumultus faciendi. Ratio The-</l>
    <l n="15">ologica est, quia ita videtur</l>
    <l n="16">provocans semetipsum vindi-</l>
    <l n="17">care velle, atque aliquâ ratio-</l>
    <l n="18">ne locum iræ relinquere, con-</l>
    <l n="19">tra monitum Apostoli. Quin</l>
    <l n="20">imò, cùm Deus voluerit in ore</l>
    <l n="21">duorum aut trium, quem con-</l>
    <l n="22">demnari posse, nisi hic semet</l>
    <l n="23">innocens submitteret, licet per</l>
    <l n="24">falsos testes convictus in legiti-</l>
    <l n="25">mo judicio, divinæ legi, ejus-</l>
    <l n="26">que ordinationi resisteret. Si</l>
    <l n="27">enim</l>
  </main_text>
